@base = http://localhost:5001

# Match-score test flow — run top to bottom (click "Send Request" above each).

### 1. Login (run first — cookie is saved automatically)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "alice", "password": "secret123"}

### 2. Save resume — partial overlap with the jobs
PUT {{base}}/api/resume
Content-Type: application/json

{"skills": ["Python", "Flask", "AWS"]}

### 3. List jobs — match_score should be filled now (Python+Flask of 5 → 40.0)
GET {{base}}/api/jobs

### 4. Create a new job — should get a match_score immediately (resume exists)
POST {{base}}/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{"description": "We are hiring a Senior Backend Engineer at Acme Corp in Austin, TX. Hybrid role. Build Python APIs with PostgreSQL, mentor juniors. 5+ years Django or Flask."}

### 5. Save resume with MORE overlap → scores should rise
PUT {{base}}/api/resume
Content-Type: application/json

{"skills": ["Python", "Flask", "PostgreSQL", "Django", "AWS"]}

### 6. List jobs again — scores should be higher now
GET {{base}}/api/jobs
